since its inception with 2013's Man of  Steel the DC extended universe  encountered obstacle after obstacle with  poor reviews mixed reaction from fans  and disappointing box office receipts  but there is one potential bright spot  on the horizon the upcoming flash solo  film which could act as a soft reboot of  the entire universe so cross your  fingers superhero fans because here's a  look at why the flash movie could fix  the DCE you flash to the rescue under  the guiding hand of director Zack Snyder  the DC EU was positioned as the dark and  gritty alternative to the bright and fun  Marvel movies but since being an  alternative to fun is a recipe for  failure  the folks at Warner Brothers have since  changed direction demoting Snyder in  promoting Walter Hamada to head of the  comic-book division in 2018 as an  attempt to lighten things up and with  the possible exception of Wonder Woman  no DC hero so far has been as bright and  upbeat as Ezra Miller's flash who added  some much-needed levity to 2017 s  Justice League if the DC EU is going to  write the ship the Flash's brand of  spunky fun may be exactly what Warner  Brothers and fans have been hoping for  flashpoint the Warner Brothers has  reportedly decided not to name the  upcoming flash film flashpoint as  originally planned it's still expected  that the movie will draw heavily from  the popular 2011 flashpoint comic book  storyline that's important because the  plot involves Barry Allen realizing he's  trapped in the wrong timeline and  teaming up with his fellow heroes to fix  time and restore reality to its true  form and that means that Warner Brothers  would have the perfect excuse to  jettison any details from their previous  DC EU films that fans and critics didn't  life things like potkins weird me first  lessons on selfishness and a morality  Superman killing Zod and the whole  Martha scene can be erased quicker and  more successfully than Henry cavils  mustache flashpoint gives Warner  Brothers a chance to totally rewrite the  history of the DC EU in order to create  a better future for its characters and  its fans the arrowverse if the plot of  flashpoint sounds familiar it might be  because the CW's flash TV series adapted  the comic for its third season storyline  and that suggests another opportunity  for the flash movie the multiverse in  the TV show of course flash and his pals  have discovered that there are lots of  alternate universes and timeline  comprising a multiverse which already  includes versions of Superman and  Supergirl among others it would be easy  and awesome for the film version of  Barry Allen to cross over and meet the  characters from the CW's arrow verse  considering flash has consistently been  one of the CW's most popular shows it's  the kind of fan service that could bring  a whole built-in audience to the  theaters and even give Warner Brothers a  rare leg up on Marvel which has  struggled to connect its TV shows to its  movies Elseworlds another benefit to  introducing the concept of the  multiverse to the DC EU is that it helps  explain not just all the previous  versions of DC super people that have  appeared on film but all the future out  of continuity movies Warner Brothers is  planning for instance it's been  announced that the upcoming Joker  standalone movie is already set to  appear in another timeline that could be  confusing for fans who just saw a new  version of Joker &amp; Suicide Squad but if  flash introduces the DC eu2 Elseworlds  the name given to alternative universe  DC superhero stories everything will  still make sense and it would also allow  Warner Brothers to recast its big roles  with more ease with Ben Affleck  constantly rumored to be leaving as  Batman having some random new dude put  on the cowl could be jarring but if it  turns out Affleck is just a wrong  version of Batman from some Elseworlds  timeline accepting a new star in the  role could be a lot easier a tradition  of successful reboots fans who object to  the idea of rebooting the DC EU through  a flashpoint event this early on would  do well to remember that this wouldn't  be the first time a superhero franchise  has been rebooted and often with great  success the x-men series repeatedly  alters its continuity within the ongoing  story the Batman franchise was  revitalized by Christopher Nolan's  trilogy and even more recently Spiderman  was reinvigorated by Marvel's Tom  Holland LED take on the character and  just like how Holland's version of  spider-man found solo success after  breaking out of Captain America Civil  War Ezra Miller's flash could do the  same following his well received  appearance in Justice League  all while resetting the elements of the  DC menu that don't work in the process  sure it would be pretty fast for a  reboot but after all nobody is faster  than the flash Godspeed Barry Allen  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our youtube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you left too  [Music]
 

